    "doi": "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-026-42072-3",
    "abstract": "Studying the temporal and spatial variations of potential evapotranspiration (ET<sub>0</sub>) in the Hexi Corridor region and its response to climatic factors is of great significance for improving the utilization efficiency of agricultural water resources. The temporal and spatial characteristics of ET<sub>0</sub> and the six meteorological factors influencing the variation of ET<sub>0</sub> in the FAO P-M formula during 1960-2019 have been revealed based on the statistical analysis method and the spatial interpolation method. Qualitative methods such as principal component analysis, cluster analysis, and grey relational grade were organically combined with quantitative methods such as sensitivity analysis and contribution rate calculation to comprehensively and objectively reveal the response relationship of ET<sub>0</sub> to climate factors. The results showed that ET<sub>0</sub> in the Hexi corridor showed a fluctuating increase during the period 1960-2019, and the change points were 1969 and 2002, respectively. ET<sub>0</sub> increased from the southeast to the northwest, with a range from 812.3 to 1516.6 mm. Temperature factors such as R<sub>n</sub>, T<sub>mean</sub>, T<sub>max,</sub> and T<sub>min</sub>, change closely with ET<sub>0</sub>, followed by humidity and wind speed factors. The increase in ET<sub>0</sub> is the most sensitive to the decrease in R<sub>n</sub>, followed by the decrease in u<sub>2</sub> and the increase in T<sub>mean</sub>. Increasing T<sub>mean</sub> was the main reason for increasing ET<sub>0</sub>, followed by u<sub>2</sub> and R<sub>n</sub>, and the combined contribution of the six meteorological factors was 72.39% during 1960-2019. This study has revealed the response of ET<sub>0</sub> to climate factors, providing a scientific reference for more rational planning and efficient utilization of water resources in arid and semi-arid regions.",
    "field": "Hydrometeorology",
    "problem": "Previous analyses of potential evapotranspiration (ET\u2080) variations are often not comprehensive as they focus only on quantitative attribution, revealing the complex relationship with meteorological factors from a single aspect, which is insufficient to provide a complete and objective understanding.",
    "method": "This study combines qualitative methods, such as principal component and cluster analysis, with quantitative methods, like sensitivity and contribution rate analysis, to reveal the relationship between potential evapotranspiration and meteorological variables in the Hexi corridor.",
    "task": "The task is to qualitatively and quantitatively analyze the relationship between spatiotemporal variations of potential evapotranspiration (ET\u2080) and meteorological variables in the Hexi corridor of Northwest China to understand its response to climate factors.",
