            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "Located in Gansu Province at the northern foothills of the Qilian Mountains in northwestern China, the Hexi Corridor (37\u00b015'-42\u00b069'N, 92\u00b027'-104\u00b020'W) is about 1,000 km long and its area is about 2.26\u00d7105 km\u00b2. It is a concentrated planting area of cash crops in Gansu Province and an irreplaceable commercial grain base in China [26]. The Hexi Corridor consists of three inland basins, the Shiyang River basin in the east, the Heihe River basin in the center and the Shule River basin in the west. It belongs to the typical temperate and warm temperate continental climate, with climatic characteristics of drought, little rain, strong evaporation, significant temperature differences between day and night, and abundant light.",
