            "target_entity_instance": "Hexi Corridor",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "Changes in soil water holding capacity greatly affect vegetation growth. Therefore, evapotranspiration is a critical factor in the development of irrigation water regimes in a scientific and rational way[5,6]. Changes in evapotranspiration have an impact on soil water storage, surface runoff, and underground runoff, which in turn causes changes in groundwater levels, affecting vegetation and crop growth. Therefore, precipitation, evapotranspiration, soil water storage, and groundwater level are interrelated and affect each other as an integral whole, and they are all important links in the hydrological cycle. The water budget imbalance caused by precipitation and evapotranspiration is the main cause of meteorological drought, hydrological drought, and agricultural drought. Therefore, ET\u2080 is a critical factor in drought monitoring and evaluation [7].",
